20) Use of new Keyword

The new keyword is used to create an object and allocate memory.

Example
class Student {
}

public class Demo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Student s = new Student();
    }
}

Here:

new Student() creates a new object.
Memory is allocated.
The constructor is called automatically.
